.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt VAINFO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vainfo
.Nd display information from VA API driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a
.Op Fl -display Ar x11 | wayland | drm | help
.Op Fl -device Ar node
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     This program displays information from about the VA API driver
     installed in the system.
.Ed
.Pp
.Nm
opens a VA display, through Wayland, X11 or a DRM node in that order
unless
.Fl -display
names one, loads the driver libva chooses for the device, and prints
libva's version, the driver's name and version, and each profile the
driver supports with its entry points:
.Dv VAEntrypointVLD
for decoding,
.Dv VAEntrypointEncSlice
for encoding and
.Dv VAEntrypointVideoProc
for video processing.
.Bl -tag -width "--display display"
.It Fl a , Fl -all
Print every attribute of each profile and entry point as well.
.It Fl -display Ar display
Use the display named, or list the displays this build has with
.Ar help .
.It Fl -device Ar node
Open the DRM node, such as
.Pa /dev/dri/renderD128 ,
with the drm display.
.It Fl -help
Print the usage.
.El
.Pp
On Rach2 the GNU root has Intel's i965 driver, which libva loads for the
i915 driver's render node after looking for Intel's media driver, which the
root does not have; on Haswell it decodes MPEG-2, H.264, VC-1 and JPEG, as
.Xr i915 4
describes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vainfo --display drm --device /dev/dri/renderD128
.Ed
.Sh RACH2
The description is Debian's manual, which has no other text, rendered
from the pinned package; the rest is Rach2's.
The package's copyright and license terms are installed under
.Pa /usr/share/doc/vainfo/copyright .
